10:# Granite Switch 4.1 8B (revision 4.1.1)
12:📝 **Read the launch blog:** [Granite Switch 4.1.1: Update models like you update software](http://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/granite-switch-4-1-1)
14:**Model Summary:** Granite Switch 4.1.1 8B is a modular LLM that composes a base model, multiple adapters and an encoder together so that a single hosted endpoint can move between natural-language responses, general and specialized decisions, and speech-to-text.
16:Adapters are activated on demand via control tokens in the chat template. For full details on model composition and adapter configuration, see [BUILD.md](BUILD.md).
18:- **Base Model:** `ibm-granite/granite-4.1-8b` (8B params, 128K context)
19:- **Adapters:** 2 — `decision` (aLoRA, general-purpose Decisions, updated weights in 4.1.1) and `guardian-core` (aLoRA, from `granitelib-guardian-r1.0`)
24:- **Automatically Composed with:** [granite-switch](https://github.com/generative-computing/granite-switch) 0.1.1
26:Granite Switch is also available in [granite-switch-4.1-30b](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-switch-4.1-30b) (same Chat + Decisions + Guardian + speech configuration, 30B base), and with the complete Granite Libraries bundle (no audio) in [granite-switch-4.1-8b-preview](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-switch-4.1-8b-preview), [-30b-preview](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-switch-4.1-30b-preview), and [-3b-preview](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-switch-4.1-3b-preview).
32:Revision 4.1.1 keeps the same two adapters as revision 4.1. Compared to 4.1:
