131:[Mellea](https://github.com/generative-computing/mellea) is the preferred way to run Granite Switch adapters in applications. It wraps **every adapter in the Granite Libraries family** (guardian, rag, core) as a direct operation instead of raw prompt engineering — see the full [Mellea + Granite Switch guide](https://github.com/generative-computing/granite-switch/blob/main/tutorials/guides/mellea_with_granite_switch.md) for the complete set of intrinsics (e.g. `policy_guardrails`, `factuality_detection`, if composed into a checkpoint). Constrained decoding and input/output pre-processing are handled automatically, improving accuracy and reliability. The `guardian_check` call below works unchanged for `guardian-core` in this checkpoint.
133:`decision` is now part of Granite Libraries — it ships in [`granitelib-core-r1.0`](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granitelib-core-r1.0/tree/main/decision) — but has **no Mellea intrinsic yet**: use the low-level section below for it meanwhile. Mellea support for `decision` is planned and will later collapse it to a single call too. An Adapter SDK for training your own custom and third-party adapters in [Mellea](https://docs.mellea.ai/advanced/lora-and-alora-adapters) is planned.
