67:Transcription runs on the same endpoint as chat and decisions, so you don't need a separate speech server and how the model is called doesn't change. Incoming audio is transcribed by the embedded [**Granite Speech 5.0 TurboCTC**](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc) model (470M params, non-autoregressive conformer CTC encoder; English, French, German, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian and Japanese, with punctuated and capitalized output), the fastest ASR model on the [OpenASR Leaderboard](https://huggingface.co/spaces/hf-audio/open_asr_leaderboard) <!-- TODO: add "as of <date>" -->. The language is detected from the audio, so no language parameter is needed. The transcript is spliced into the chat context in place of the audio content part. The speech encoder and the LLM are not yet jointly trained — there is no trained projection coupling them together yet; see [docs/AUDIO.md](https://github.com/generative-computing/granite-switch/blob/main/docs/AUDIO.md) in the granite-switch repo for the full design and limitations (no decode-time steering).
110:This checkpoint is produced with `granite-switch==0.1.1` by composing the base model with the aLoRA
