   200	> **Token exchange, not a hiding matrix**
   201	>
   202	> MultiSwitch does not use the group-based KV-hiding path. `grep -rn hiding src/` returns two comments and no mechanism; the control token is neutralised by having its id replaced before embedding, which is why `modified_ids` above shows `11` and `12` where the control tokens were.
   203	
   204	## 3. Latest-wins routing, and returning to base
   205	
   206	Because each position reads the value at *its own* address, and addresses only ever increase, routing is piecewise-constant and changes only at a control token. It never drifts back to base on its own.
