    10	# Granite Switch 4.1 8B (revision 4.1.1)
    11	
    12	📝 **Read the launch blog:** [Granite Switch 4.1.1: Update models like you update software](http://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/granite-switch-4-1-1)
    13	
    14	**Model Summary:** Granite Switch 4.1.1 8B is a modular LLM that composes a base model, multiple adapters and an encoder together so that a single hosted endpoint can move between natural-language responses, general and specialized decisions, and speech-to-text.
    15	
    16	Adapters are activated on demand via control tokens in the chat template. For full details on model composition and adapter configuration, see [BUILD.md](BUILD.md).
    17	
    18	- **Base Model:** `ibm-granite/granite-4.1-8b` (8B params, 128K context)
    19	- **Adapters:** 2 — `decision` (aLoRA, general-purpose Decisions, updated weights in 4.1.1) and `guardian-core` (aLoRA, from `granitelib-guardian-r1.0`)
    20	- **Audio:** embedded speech-to-text via `ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc` (470M params; English, French, German, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Japanese)
    21	- **License:** [Apache 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)
    22	- **Release Date:** October 27, 2026 (revision 4.1.1); October 14, 2026 (revision 4.1)
    23	- **Backends:** HuggingFace Transformers, vLLM
    24	- **Automatically Composed with:** [granite-switch](https://github.com/generative-computing/granite-switch) 0.1.1
    25	
===
   355	---
   356	
   357	### How It Works
   358	
   359	Granite Switch uses **coarse-grained expert switching** — one adapter is active across all layers for a contiguous span of tokens. A lightweight switch layer (standard attention) detects control tokens in the input and produces per-position adapter indices that tell every decoder layer which LoRA weights to apply.
   360	
===
   383	Key properties:
   384	
   385	- **KV cache normalization** — each adapter sees only the base model's KV cache, never another adapter's internal state
   386	- **No joint training** — adapters are developed, tested, and published independently
   387	- **Single checkpoint** — one file works with both HuggingFace and vLLM, no conversion needed
   388	- **Zero code changes** — adapter selection happens entirely through the chat template
   389	
   390	### Model Architecture
   391	
   392	**Base Model**
   393	
   394	| | |
   395	|---|---|
   396	| **Model** | [Granite 4.1 8B](https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-4.1-8b) |
   397	| **Parameters** | 8 billion |
   398	| **Context Length** | 131,072 tokens |
   399	| **Architecture** | Dense decoder-only transformer (GQA, RoPE, SwiGLU, RMSNorm) |
   400	| **Languages** | English, German, Spanish, French, Japanese, Portuguese, Arabic, Czech, Italian, Korean, Dutch, Chinese |
