   876	) -> torch.Tensor | BlockMask | None:
   877	    """
   878	    Create a standard causal mask based on the attention implementation used (stored in the config). If `past_key_values`
   879	    has a hybrid cache structure, this function will return the mask corresponding to one of the "full_attention" layers (to align
   880	    to what is needed in the `modeling_xxx.py` files).
   881	
   882	    Args:
   883	        config (`PreTrainedConfig`):
   884	            The model config.
   885	        inputs_embeds (`torch.Tensor`):
   886	            The input embeddings of shape (batch_size, query_length, hidden_dim). This is used only to infer the
   887	            batch size, query length and dtype.
   888	        attention_mask (`torch.Tensor`, optional):
   889	            The 2D attention mask corresponding to padded tokens of shape (batch_size, number_of_seen_tokens+q_length).
   890	            It can also be an already prepared 4D mask, in which case it is returned as-is.
   891	        past_key_values (`Cache`, optional):
   892	            The past key values, if we use a cache.
   893	        position_ids (`torch.Tensor`, optional)
   894	            A 2D tensor of shape (batch_size, query_length) indicating the positions of each token in the sequences.
   895	        or_mask_function (`Callable`, optional):
   896	            An optional mask function to combine with the causal mask function (by doing the union of both). This is
   897	            useful to easily overlay another mask on top of the causal one, for example for image tokens handling.
   898	        and_mask_function (`Callable`, optional):
   899	            An optional mask function to combine with the causal mask function (by doing the intersection of both). This is
   900	            useful to easily overlay another mask on top of the causal one, for example for image tokens handling.
   901	        block_sequence_ids (`torch.Tensor`, *optional*):
   902	            A tensor of same shape as input IDs indicating to which block or group each token belongs to. Tokens from
   903	            the same block will keep a bidirectional mask within the block, attending causally to the past. Index `-1`
   904	            can be used for blocks that have to keep complete causality within itself.
   905	        layer_idx (`int`, *optional*):
   906	            The cache layer to size the mask against. By default, the first "full_attention" layer is used, which is
   907	            correct whenever all layers of a given mask type have seen the same tokens. Pass it explicitly for caches
   908	            where layers of the same type hold different lengths (e.g. per-depth MTP streams).
   909	        allow_is_causal_skip (`bool`, optional):
   910	            Whether to allow returning `None` (and relying on `sdpa`'s `is_causal` argument) when the mask would be a
   911	            plain causal mask. Set to `False` to always materialize the mask, e.g. when it is later concatenated with
   912	            another mask. Defaults to `True`.
